WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.904
Graph neural networks are limited in what they can
compute, and the yardstick,

00:00:04.984 --> 00:00:06.949
the Weisfeiler-Lehman hierarchy,

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:10.910
is hard to interpret and too coarse to separate
architectures.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:17.428
This ICML 2023 paper measures a graph network
instead by which equivariant polynomials it can compute.

00:00:17.508 --> 00:00:21.006
The authors give a complete basis for these polynomials,

00:00:21.086 --> 00:00:24.073
build tools to read off any model's exact power,

00:00:24.153 --> 00:00:29.440
and design a stronger network that reaches state of
the art on molecular benchmarks.
